\title{bricks: Backend-Agnostic Databricks Data Access}
\description{
A small, unified interface for reading data from Databricks in R, regardless of how you connect. The same handful of verbs work across a Databricks SQL warehouse (via 'DBI' and 'odbc'), a native 'sparklyr' session inside a Databricks notebook, a remote Databricks Connect session (via 'pysparklyr'), and a local CSV extract. Table and SQL handles stay lazy so filters, joins, and aggregations push down to Databricks compute, and a single collect step pulls a local tibble.
